      "originalText": "day 5 - rendering form handling: in this class i \nlearnt form handling with two differnet methods\nbruteforce approach and better approach. \nI created three different form componenet form1, form2, \nand form3 then form1 I wrote form inside 3 input\n1st for name, 2nd for email and 3rd for password\nthen i worte onChange() on form then I given callback inside\nthe onChange then I chane e value and console e \nthen I got synthetic Event. then i check in synthetic \nevent inside i see targert object inside value \nthen i wrote e.target.value after console i got \nactual input. then i store this value inside the \nname state, email in email state and passwond in \npassword state. then I print this values on ui\nusing   h1 tag \n<h1>Name - {name}</h1>\n      <h1>Email - {email}</h1>\n      <h1>Password - {pass}</h1>\nthis is for bruateforce approach form1 component\nalso for better approach in form2\ni create only one state that is formData \nthen i wrote on every input filed         \nonChange={(e) => setFormData({...formData, name: e.target.value})}\n and print result on ui using\n<h1>Name - {formData.name}</h1>\n    <h1>Email - {formData.email}</h1>\n    <h1>Password - {formData.pass}</h1>\n\nand another modificaiton on better approach is \ni create a function handclick and pass into onChange for call>\n let handleClick = (e) => {\n    let { name, value } = e.target;\n    setFormData({ ...formData, [name]: value });\n  };\n\nand get all value in name of input and update the state\nand same print on ui. \n\nalso on app.jsx componenet I wrote user name state and pass object \n{name: \"vaibhav\"} then using button onClick  change the object to different name\nit's only change the name when click the button after stop the changing object. \nbecuase state function compare previous value == upadeting value so it's\nchange only once. \n\n <h1>User - {user.name}</h1>\n      <button onClick={() => user.name = \"Akshay\"}>Change Name</button> \n also i this class i learnt how to implement tailwindcss in \nour react-vite project I first run command npm install tailwindcss @tailwindcss/vite\nthen i installed tailwindcss packages then on index.css i \nremove external styling a wrote @import 'tailwindcss'\nthen on vite.config.js file i import the tailwindcss and inside the \nplugin object i called tailwindcss. \nthen I used different class inside my form\nlike text-xl, text-red-500, flex, flex-col, justify-center,\nitems-center, border, border-white, rounded, w-40, w-full,\nh-screen, bg-black, gap-4, and lot of things i learnt tailwindcss classes.  \n\n\n\n\n\n",
